remediation:
1. Configure web server to block access to composer.json and composer.lock files

2. Apache (.htaccess):
   <FilesMatch "^composer\.(json|lock)$">
       Order allow,deny
       Deny from all
   </FilesMatch>

3. Nginx configuration:
   location ~ /composer\.(json|lock)$ {
       deny all;
       access_log off;
       log_not_found off;
   }

4. Remove composer files from web-accessible directories if not needed in production

5. Implement .gitignore rules to prevent accidental commits of composer files to public repositories

6. Use environment variables and separate configuration files for production dependencies instead of storing in web root

7. Regularly audit web-accessible files to ensure no sensitive configuration files are exposed
